Supported. The paper defines the semantic discriminative loss as an InfoNCE-style softmax cross-entropy over in-batch pairs:

L_semantic = -(1/N) Σ_i log { exp(f_i^v · f_i^t / τ) / Σ_j exp(f_i^v · f_j^t / τ) }

This uses a softmax over all text embeddings in the batch (negatives included). The text describes the goal as maximizing cosine similarity for positives and minimizing it for negatives, but the actual logits use a dot product (no explicit normalization is stated; if embeddings are normalized, the dot product equals cosine similarity). Therefore, it does not directly maximize cosine similarity alone; it uses softmax cross-entropy with negatives. If any prior statement implied direct cosine maximization without the softmax/negatives, retract it.
